Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}From NVIDIA Research at CVPR 2023,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.86,0:00:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}this work closes a safety-critical gap in object pose estimation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.36,0:00:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Standard two-stage pipelines detect keypoints, then solve for the 6D pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.49,0:00:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but give no guarantee on how wrong the answer might be.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.30,0:00:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors add two pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.18,0:00:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Conformal keypoint detection turns heatmap detections into circular or elliptical prediction
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.55,0:00:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}sets that provably cover the true keypoints with a chosen probability,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.41,0:00:30.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}say ninety percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.72,0:00:37.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Geometric uncertainty propagation pushes those sets through the geometry to form a Pose Uncertainty Set,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.93,0:00:40.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or PURSE, covering the true pose.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.22,0:00:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}From PURSE they compute an average pose and use semidefinite relaxation to bound the worst-case error.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.29,0:00:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On LineMOD Occlusion, coverage is valid and the bounds hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.75,0:00:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Estimating an object's 6D pose from an image underlies augmented reality,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.54,0:01:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}autonomous driving, robotic manipulation, and space robotics.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.53,0:01:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The dominant recipe is two stages: first detect semantic keypoints,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.93,0:01:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then recover the pose by minimizing reprojection error through Perspective-n-Points.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.43,0:01:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}These methods score well on benchmarks,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.99,0:01:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet they return a single pose with no statement about how trustworthy it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.97,0:01:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For safety-critical systems that is a serious gap: no guarantee on the keypoints,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.28,0:01:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}no guarantee the optimizer found the right pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.43,0:01:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and no formal bound on the worst-case error against the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.79,0:01:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Why is this hard?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.00,0:01:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors name three challenges.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.42,0:01:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, neural keypoint detectors can be arbitrarily wrong, producing outliers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.98,0:01:44.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, rejecting those outliers is a nonconvex optimization;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.32,0:01:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}fast heuristics like RANSAC are common but cannot guarantee global optimality and can fail silently.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.44,0:01:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, and most fundamental, there is no provably correct uncertainty quantification,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.49,0:02:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}no formal worst-case error bound between estimate and groundtruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.19,0:02:09.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Certifying that the optimizer is globally optimal still gives no probabilistic guarantee on the pose itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper delivers exactly that guarantee, end to end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.10,0:02:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method has two stages.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.86,0:02:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In conformal keypoint detection,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.02,0:02:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a calibration set of labeled images gives nonconformity scores for the heatmap detector.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.97,0:02:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Two designs are offered: a peak score,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.54,0:02:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the scaled distance from the true keypoint to the most probable pixel,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.28,0:02:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a covariance score, a Mahalanobis distance over top detections,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.81,0:02:38.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yielding circular and elliptical sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.38,0:02:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Sorting the scores gives a threshold so each true keypoint lies in its set with probability one minus epsilon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.82,0:02:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In geometric uncertainty propagation,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.32,0:02:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}these sets become quadratic constraints on the pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.83,0:02:54.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}defining the Pose Uncertainty Set.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.13,0:02:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Since it is nonconvex, RANSAG samples three keypoints,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.79,0:03:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}solves the minimal P3P problem, keeps poses inside the set, and averages them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.06,0:03:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Finally, maximizing the distance to the farthest pose still inside PURSE,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.00,0:03:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}relaxed as a semidefinite program,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.30,0:03:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}certifies worst-case rotation and translation bounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.18,0:03:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The results confirm the theory on three fronts.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.01,0:03:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, coverage is valid: at a ninety percent target,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.85,0:03:25.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}empirical coverage across objects sits right around ninety percent and tightens as the calibration set grows.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.68,0:03:29.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.51,0:03:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the bounds are correct: in scatter plots of certified bound versus actual error,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.34,0:03:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}every case where PURSE covers the true pose stays below the diagonal,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.18,0:03:40.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the bound is never violated when the guarantee holds.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.01,0:03:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, the average pose is accurate,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.84,0:03:48.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}beating prior methods on the two-dimensional projection metric with groundtruth boxes
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.68,0:03:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and staying comparable with Faster-RCNN detections.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.81,0:04:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message: you can turn a standard two-stage pose estimator into one that tells you how wrong it might be,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.17,0:04:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with a real statistical guarantee, and pay little in accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.10,0:04:07.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Conformal prediction supplies coverage on the keypoints,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.65,0:04:10.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}geometry propagates it to the pose as PURSE,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.44,0:04:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and semidefinite relaxation converts the set into concrete worst-case bounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.32,0:04:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because it wraps any heatmap keypoint detector,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.30,0:04:23.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the approach points toward provably correct perception wherever safety matters.
